cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DeltScan, please cite the software below and the accompanying article."
title: "DeltScan: fidelity bounds and a single-grid convergence protocol for extreme-event statistics in integrable turbulence"
abstract: >-
  DeltScan accompanies a methodological study of spurious extreme events in
  under-resolved split-step Fourier simulations of integrable turbulence. It
  provides a symmetrized split-step Fourier integrator for the focusing
  nonlinear Schrodinger equation with random initial data, a single-grid
  low-pass ("delta") fingerprint diagnostic that separates aliasing artefacts
  from resolved peaks, an ensemble driver with checkpointing, and bootstrap
  statistics for the ensemble medians and tail probabilities.
